{"id": "EUVD-2022-56044", "enisaUuid": "dc658558-58c9-315d-af64-fbfac1bd1aed", "description": "PocketMine-MP before 4.0.6 does not validate facing values in PlayerActionPacket (for START_BREAK and CRACK_BREAK actions) or in UseItemTransactionData (typically within InventoryTransactionPacket). A remote authenticated attacker can send crafted packets with invalid facing values (e.g., negative or out-of-range) to crash the server, resulting in a denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-09-07T12:55:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-08T15:20:57", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/pmmp/PocketMine-MP/security/advisories/GHSA-xh99-hw7h-wf63", "https://github.com/pmmp/PocketMine-MP/commit/f126479c37ff00a717a828f5271cf8e821d12d6c", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/pocketmine-mp-before-4.0.6-denial-of-service-via-playeractionpacket"], "aliases": ["CVE-2022-51015", "GHSA-jqrm-67hm-q329"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.68, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a2b79aa3-848f-372d-ac92-caf56a5ce396", "product": {"name": "PocketMine-MP", "vendor": {"name": "pmmp"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.0.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "00a6fed1-db19-3dea-9ae9-736e65e9144b", "vendor": {"name": "pmmp"}}], "isExploited": false}